  "note": "Election of the whole council (21 members, seven for each of the Central, East and West wards) on 15 January 1923. All 21 seats were filled without a contest (Belfast News-Letter, 10 and 13 January 1923). The Nationalists, who held a large majority in the ward, nominated nobody. The result report gives the new council as 20 Unionists and 1 Nationalist, although the nomination report labels all 21 as Unionists; the discrepancy is left as printed. Returned unopposed."
